In general, yeah, that's pretty normal.

Finding a WoW is very rare so not finding one in two months is quite
normal.

Getting a wish from a fountain is also pretty rare: quaffing from a
non-magical fountain (6/7 of all fountains) you have a 1/30 chance of
getting a water demon who then has an 80+DL/100 chance of being
hostile. If the demon is not hostile, he'll grant you a wish. So, for
example, you see a fountain on DL3. There is a 2.37% chance it will
give you a wish. Dipping items into fountains seems to remove the need
for a magical fountain (is this correct?) and so you have a slightly
higher 2.76% chance of getting a wish.

And you really need to take into account the risk factor of quaffing
from/dipping into fountains - I only try them if i can reliably handle
all the negative side effects or if i'm in a position that is somewhat
dire and i need a miracle anyways.

A more common source of wishes for me is the light store in minetown -
there is fairly often a magic lamp there.

